module gunbc.fn_arrow_skeleton_unprojected_leaf_seed_growth

import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// FORWARD-FREEZE RECEIPT for the hand Rust the MQ-2 cutover adds to the host fn-arrow skeleton
// marshal. v1_compiler.coproduct_reflection marshal_generic emitted an EMPTY Conj for every
// expression it does not project (an int literal, a non-parameter variable), and
// v2.std.compilers.body_lowering application_read -- which replaced v2.std.node_query node_is_call
// / call_callee_target / call_argument_targets -- refuses an empty Conj operand as surface residue.
// Left alone, every call with such an argument would refuse and the v2.std.fn_index call walk
// (and effect_reach, live_read_classification, determinism behind it) would be Unestablished over
// almost the whole corpus. Admitting the empty Conj instead would be the absorbing fallback DESIGN
// section 5 forbids: residue passing as an operand.
//
// ONE ARM, ONE HELPER, POSITIONS KEPT. unprojected_leaf_record builds the exact shape
// node_is_unprojected_leaf admits, and marshal_generic takes it only where it previously built a
// Conj with no edges. The marker spelling comes from the generated constant
// (gunbc.fn_arrow_skeleton_seed_constants_emit), not a literal in the seed.
data fn_arrow_skeleton_unprojected_leaf_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.coproduct_reflection", decl_name: "unprojected_leaf_record", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "The host fn-arrow skeleton marshal represented an unprojected expression as an empty Conj, which is the residue shape v2.std.compilers.body_lowering application_read refuses as an operand. Cutting the call readers over to application_read (MQ-2) therefore needs the host marshal to say 'unprojected' in a shape the reader can tell apart from residue: a Conj with one Named edge (body_view_unprojected_leaf_marker) over an empty Conj, which node_is_unprojected_leaf admits and application_read surfaces as UnprojectedOperand. A consumer that needs such an operand's content refuses, located; a genuine empty Conj still refuses. No other marshal behaviour changes and every operand keeps its slot.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "fn-arrow skeletons are produced by the v2 body-lowering route (body_producer_forward), so no host marshal constructs call operands. Owned by MQ-5 of adhoc-1b3dbcdb-f9f (gentle-koi-724): the replacing carrier is the v2 lowered value (BodyValueLowering Lowered/Carried) that body_producer_forward emits per source child slot. That route is what deletes this row; a further edit to marshal_generic would not.",
  current_boundary: "Unprojected expressions in host fn-arrow skeletons are typed opaque leaves: the call walk reads the call and its callee and carries the argument as uninspectable. A reader that must inspect such an argument -- the no_dual_representation alpha check on a first argument -- reports EqOperandUnreadable rather than guessing."
}
